1
00:00:00,150 --> 00:00:03,239
Millions of small shops already sell with a PayPal button.

2
00:00:03,239 --> 00:00:05,635
But AI shopping agents can't really use them.

3
00:00:05,635 --> 00:00:08,564
They have to guess their way through buttons and forms.

4
00:00:08,564 --> 00:00:10,800
ShopBridge fixes that with one script tag.

5
00:00:11,704 --> 00:00:15,875
Here is Lin's Tea Corner, an ordinary little shop with PayPal checkout.

6
00:00:15,875 --> 00:00:19,694
Ask Chrome's WebMCP API for tools on this page, and you get zero.

7
00:00:20,595 --> 00:00:23,850
Now the same page with one ShopBridge script tag.

8
00:00:23,850 --> 00:00:27,371
It reads the product data the shop already publishes,

9
00:00:27,371 --> 00:00:29,564
and registers seven WebMCP tools:

10
00:00:29,564 --> 00:00:34,015
search, product details, cart, checkout, order status, and capture.

11
00:00:34,920 --> 00:00:39,208
The readiness report loads both pages live and scores them in AG Grid.

12
00:00:39,208 --> 00:00:41,413
The original shop scores forty-five.

13
00:00:41,413 --> 00:00:43,250
After conversion, one hundred.

14
00:00:44,151 --> 00:00:45,208
Now an AI agent.

15
00:00:45,208 --> 00:00:46,001
The request:

16
00:00:46,001 --> 00:00:48,841
buy two bags of jasmine tea and one oolong.

17
00:00:48,841 --> 00:00:51,087
GLM 4.7 Flash planned these calls,

18
00:00:51,087 --> 00:00:55,117
and each one runs as a real WebMCP tool inside the live page.

19
00:00:55,117 --> 00:00:58,618
We cut the model's thinking time from this recording.

20
00:00:58,618 --> 00:01:03,308
The agent searches, fills the cart, and creates a PayPal sandbox order.

21
00:01:03,308 --> 00:01:04,893
It never pays by itself.

22
00:01:04,893 --> 00:01:06,941
It hands back an approval link.

23
00:01:07,847 --> 00:01:12,398
The human buyer opens that link and approves the payment in the PayPal sandbox,

24
00:01:12,398 --> 00:01:13,608
using a test account.

25
00:01:13,608 --> 00:01:15,625
Everything in this demo is sandbox.

26
00:01:15,625 --> 00:01:16,777
No real money moves.

27
00:01:17,678 --> 00:01:20,331
Back in the shop, the order is now approved,

28
00:01:20,331 --> 00:01:22,683
so the capture order tool completes it.

29
00:01:22,683 --> 00:01:23,105
Status:

30
00:01:23,105 --> 00:01:25,638
completed, with a real sandbox capture ID.

31
00:01:26,540 --> 00:01:31,880
Under the hood, prices are always recomputed on the server from the shop's own catalog,

32
00:01:31,880 --> 00:01:35,011
and the PayPal client refuses any non-sandbox host.

33
00:01:35,011 --> 00:01:38,325
We built this from the public PayPal and WebMCP specs,

34
00:01:38,325 --> 00:01:40,719
without official Store Sync onboarding.

35
00:01:40,719 --> 00:01:43,604
Unlike AutoShop, a permission layer for agents,

36
00:01:43,604 --> 00:01:46,735
ShopBridge retrofits shops that already use PayPal.

37
00:01:46,735 --> 00:01:49,190
The code and live demo are linked below.
